<section id="no-remote-reset" aria-labelledby="no-reset-heading" class="content-defer border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-white py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/60 p-6 sm:p-10 lg:p-12">
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
                <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-amber-100 px-3.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-900">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation text-amber-700" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span>03 • No Remote Reset &amp; Risk Management</span>
                </div>

                <h2 id="no-reset-heading" class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">
                    Why PassKee Has No "Forgot Password" Button
                </h2>

                <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
                    If a service can reset your password by sending an email link, it holds the ability to access your account without your keys. Because PassKee is zero-knowledge and never stores your Master Password or Emergency Secret Key, <strong>we cannot reset your credentials or recover a locked vault remotely.</strong>
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-2xs">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700">Scenario A</span>
                        <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-800">Full Access</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="mt-2 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Signing In on a New Device</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                        Enter your Email, Master Password, and the <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">PK-XXXX-...</code> Emergency Secret Key you copied during registration to decrypt your vault immediately.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-2xs">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-700">Scenario B</span>
                        <span class="rounded-full bg-amber-100 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-amber-900">Backup via KDBX</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="mt-2 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Lost Secret Key, Active Session Open</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                        If you still have an unlocked session on an authorized device, open Vault Actions (<code class="font-mono text-slate-800">⋮</code>) &rarr; <strong>Backup (Export to KeePass .kdbx)</strong>, then register a new account and import that <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">.kdbx</code> file.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-2xs">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700">Scenario C</span>
                        <span class="rounded-full bg-rose-100 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-rose-800">Unrecoverable</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="mt-2 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Lost Password or Key With No Active Session</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                        If you lose your Master Password or your Emergency Secret Key and have no signed-in device to export a backup, your encrypted vault remains permanently unreadable.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-amber-300/80 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6">
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-900">
                    3 Practical Ways to Safeguard Your Emergency Secret Key &amp; Vault
                </h3>
                <ul class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-print text-sky-600 mt-1 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span><strong>Store offline right after sign-up:</strong> Write down or print your <code class="font-mono text-xs">PK-XXXX-...</code> Secret Key and keep it in a physical safe or locked drawer.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-export text-emerald-600 mt-1 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span><strong>Keep periodic .kdbx backups:</strong> Use <strong>Backup &rarr; Export to KeePass (.kdbx)</strong> to save an encrypted KDBX 4 snapshot on an offline USB drive.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-ban text-rose-600 mt-1 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span><strong>Keep both factors separate:</strong> Never store your Master Password and Emergency Secret Key together in an unencrypted note or email.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
